# Own preparation procedure and later custody boundary

Actual owner `/root/research_architect`; public-only preparation, 2026-10-10 UTC. `solver-r1.py` is an independently authored strict task parser and explicit frame/event interpreter. `recursive-simulator-r1.py` is a second, recursively structured fresh-trace simulator that does not import the frame machine. It assumes public-parser-valid programs and supplies a separately traversed complete fresh trace/state/phase, not a second parser or independent checkpoint validator. Both implementations share this author's model and interpretation of the same public text. The manually reasoned fixture supplies a nine-event trace, two exact intermediate snapshots, an actual replay/failure trace, and four smaller programs; it is not a candidate or twelve-family prototype.

The runner must first verify all frozen live bytes and archived copies, then import the test source. Sources, fixtures, this procedure, configuration, runner, six operative public documents and R2 root freeze are archived before the first import/test/execution. The freeze does not contain its own hash. Its independently supplied expected SHA binds the invocation. Each attempt has new output paths and is retained, including a failure. If a source/fixture correction is necessary, preserve the old version and make new versioned files and a new freeze before importing the correction. Never revise a completed attempt or failure output.

## Explicit task requirements exercised now

Exact types/shapes and argument references, all declared call-DAG branches/unused options, simultaneous argument binding, retained frame copies, selected branch retention, advanced caller cursors, entry/exit timing, exact after-state effects, branch normalization, history-prefix equality, original-history-before-checkpoint error precedence, mode semantics, budgets including zero and terminal-at-boundary, and noncommitting next-event prediction come from `RSM_OPTION_RESUMPTION_V1.md`. The manual replay case actually repeats a committed nonzero addition after root entry passes and shows a different terminal state/status. The X-style toy changes the pending branch copy of a saved argument while preserving history. It must be invalid before any event. Other hand programs deliberately omit cohort requirements such as minimum option/parameter counts; they calibrate the public task interpreter, not the configured cohort.

The independent recursive trace plus every original-event cut/budget tests suffix composition. A manual snapshot anchors actual branch/caller structure so checkpoint checking is not justified solely by comparing the frame machine with itself. Exact per-row outputs are deterministic under the public task semantics; there are no alternative plan ties. The raw JSON parser rejects duplicate keys and nonfinite numbers as a conservative review choice to preserve typed unambiguous input; these malformed encodings are not extra corpus acceptance requirements inferred from the public record interface.

## Separately authorized future input-only stage

No future input view is read in this preparation. The proposed 216 rows and twelve families are design arithmetic only. After a separate root authorization, bind and archive the entire supplied target-free view, its actual strip/custody receipt, the exact public sources and this own source before execution. Confirm row uniqueness, precise permitted-field set, typed task extraction and exact renderer/task/split/lineage joins; don't infer family coordinates from private ID spelling. Parse each actual student-visible `Task JSON` under the public prompt boundary, recompute all 216 full typed outputs, inspect every family/context and freeze all own input predictions and first input judgments with actual identities, record/input hashes and actual completed execution. Prior own predictions may be consulted only after fresh exact joins/recomputation, with exposure disclosure. Stop before actual canonical targets, private metadata, other reviewers' first judgments or fresh formal/producer implementation/results.

This source is preparation, not a blanket trust certificate. Any unseen valid input outside calibrated cases requires manual inspection or a new source/version/calibration before using a prediction. CPU exact finite execution is appropriate for the configured event/instruction bounds; the implementation uses Python recursion for syntax validation and full fresh simulation, so no unbounded-depth interpreter claim is made.

## Later canonical adjudication, also separately authorized

After all own input predictions/firsts and independent expert/red firsts freeze and actual FINAL reviews are authorized, independently join full record hashes and full PENDING candidate bytes to raw manifest/source bindings. Preserve first/final reviewer scopes and correction failures; don't adopt their verdict as an instruction. Verify all nine named relations, owner coordinates including valid nonmember owners, the renderer-member exception, exact typed semantics/prefix/state/status, optional truthful locators/metrics, whole prospective schedule/profile/split and three normalized novelty views against actual target-free legacy inputs. Normalize name/property consistently; do not require private control-ID grammar, optional annotations, a closed descriptor tag vocabulary or unpublished manifest top-level keys. Canonical `pair_record_hashes` must remain forbidden; optional external ordered member hashes are independently checked. Resolve the supplied safe manifest path using actual raw bytes; bind the original candidate SHA externally without circular manifest hashes in candidates.

No metadata parser/corpus checker, canonical record validation, actual novelty audit, actual family/split count, expert/red evidence review or publication eligibility is executed here. Those require separately authorized fresh evidence and source freezes. Per-row correctness and whole-cohort publication eligibility must be reported separately.

## Independence and limits

This author designed the original task/curriculum and publicly reviewed the metadata amendments; common root guidance and any later adjudicator overlap are disclosed. Prior own legacy and multi-track exposure remains; no legacy canonical target, new producer/private checker, future candidate/gold or another reviewer's future initial verdict was read for this preparation. A second control structure authored by the same model does not establish human or model-independent verification. Exposed development families, finite supplied programs, repeated matched contexts and possible superficial status/format/length associations remain future measured risks, not cleared by hand tests. No sealed evaluation, model architecture, training or efficacy claim, data approval or publication authority is supplied.
